# CLAUDE.md (template — copy me)

This is a **template**, not a live instructions file. `.gitignore` excludes
`CLAUDE.md` itself (along with `AGENTS.md`, `.claude/`, `.cursor/`,
`.clinerules/`, `.gemini/`, `.windsurfrules`, `opencode.json` — every
tool-specific agent config file this project has seen), because this project
treats those as personal, per-checkout tooling preference, not shared repo
content — the same bucket as `.vscode/` or `.prettierrc`. See
[docs/llm_onboarding.md](docs/llm_onboarding.md)'s "Agent config files stay
local" section for why.

If you use Claude Code and want this orientation loaded automatically in
every session in your checkout, copy this file over the gitignored name:

```bash
cp CLAUDE.md.template CLAUDE.md
```

It will not be committed, will not show up in `git status` as a change to
push, and is yours to edit freely per checkout.

---

iSH-AOK is a heavily-diverged fork of
[ish-app/ish](https://github.com/ish-app/ish) — a Linux syscall emulator that
runs as an iOS app, JIT-translating i386/amd64/arm64/riscv64 guest code. See
[README.md](README.md) for what this fork adds on top of upstream.

Before doing substantive work here, read
**[docs/llm_onboarding.md](docs/llm_onboarding.md)**. It exists specifically
to get an LLM coding agent oriented fast in this tree: the regression suite,
debugging with no guest-side debugger, the `docs/TODO.md` collaboration
workflow, and the footguns that have already cost real time here. Treat it
as required reading before touching tests, debugging, the build, or
licensing-sensitive code — not just optional background.

The five things that matter most, before anything else:

1. **This is a fork.** Upstream's README, issues, branches and workflows are
   not this repo's. If you use `gh`, pass `--repo emkey1/ish-AOK` or it
   resolves to upstream.
2. **Check `docs/TODO.md` and `git log origin/working` before starting
   work** — someone, or some other session, may already be on it. See
   `docs/llm_onboarding.md` for the exact claim/complete workflow this
   project uses there.
3. **`meson test -C build` is host-only and thin.** The real regression gate
   is the guest suite (`tests/manual/`, run inside a booted guest via
   `/AOK/tests/setup-regressions.sh`) — CI does not run it. Don't call a
   change tested when only the host tests passed.
4. **Never regenerate a vendored `config.h`** (bash/zsh/OpenSSH) to silence a
   GCC-only warning — guard the specific site with `!__linux__` instead, or
   you'll move what ships on Darwin to fix a platform that doesn't ship.
5. **Registration is silent.** A test, doc, or native program not listed in
   its manifest/registry (`fs/aok-*.manifest`,
   `tests/manual/setup-regressions.sh`, `kernel/native.c`) is just absent on
   device — no error, no failed build.
